            <header class="lesson-header"><span class="lesson-number">Lesson 15</span><h1>API Gateway Pattern</h1><div class="lesson-meta"><span class="lesson-duration"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"/></svg>25 min</span><span class="lesson-level advanced">Advanced</span></div></header>
            <div class="lesson-body">
                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>What is an API Gateway?</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-text">Client → API Gateway → Microservices

┌────────────┐      ┌─────────────────────────────┐
│   Client   │ ───► │       API Gateway           │
└────────────┘      │  - Routing                  │
                    │  - Authentication           │
                    │  - Rate Limiting            │
                    │  - Load Balancing           │
                    └────┬────────┬────────┬──────┘
                         │        │        │
                         ▼        ▼        ▼
                    ┌────────┐ ┌────────┐ ┌────────┐
                    │ Orders │ │  Users │ │Products│
                    └────────┘ └────────┘ └────────┘</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Gateway Responsibilities</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Routing:</strong> Route requests to appropriate services</li>
                        <li><strong>Aggregation:</strong> Combine responses from multiple services</li>
                        <li><strong>Authentication:</strong> Verify tokens before forwarding</li>
                        <li><strong>Rate Limiting:</strong> Protect services from overload</li>
                        <li><strong>Caching:</strong> Cache common responses</li>
                        <li><strong>SSL Termination:</strong> Handle HTTPS at the edge</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Options for .NET</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>YARP:</strong> Microsoft's reverse proxy (.NET native)</li>
                        <li><strong>Ocelot:</strong> .NET API Gateway</li>
                        <li><strong>Kong:</strong> Popular open-source gateway</li>
                        <li><strong>Azure API Management:</strong> Managed service</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>

                <LessonTakeaways>
                    <LessonTakeaway>API Gateway is single entry point for clients.</LessonTakeaway>
                    <LessonTakeaway>Handles cross-cutting concerns centrally.</LessonTakeaway>
                    <LessonTakeaway>YARP is the recommended choice for .NET.</LessonTakeaway>
                </LessonTakeaways>
            </div>
